.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt RACH2 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rach2
.Nd an educational operating system for the 32-bit PC
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Rach2 is an educational operating system for the 32-bit x86 PC.
Its kernel is freestanding C89 and uses no libgcc.
The userland includes the ported musl C library, BusyBox shell and tools,
Dropbear SSH server, TinyCC compiler, pdpmake, and project programs
described in sections 1 and 8 of this manual.
TinyCC is installed as
.Pa /bin/tcc
and
.Pa /bin/cc ;
pdpmake is installed as
.Pa /bin/make .
.Pp
The system can rebuild its own kernel.
Images with the compiler include
.Pa /src/rach2 ,
.Pa /src/utils ,
and
.Pa /src/ish ,
each with a
.Pa guest.mk
for pdpmake.
.Ss Boot
Rach2 boots through Multiboot1, using QEMU's
.Fl kernel
option or GRUB from a disk or USB stick.
The test, os-simple, os-real, and recovery images use a KRFFS root in memory.
A disk root is a KRFFS or ext2 partition, selected by identity with
.Ql rach2.root=
on the kernel command line.
See
.Xr disk 7
for identities and
.Pa rach2/Readme.md
in the source tree for the kernel command line.
.Ql rach2.rescue
starts the kernel debug shell instead of
.Pa /sbin/init .
.Ss File systems and devices
Rach2 reads and writes FAT32, exFAT, ext2, and KRFFS, its native file
system.
ext2 supports hard and symbolic links.
A file system in a regular file can be mounted using the devices
.Pa /dev/loop0
through
.Pa /dev/loop3 ;
see
.Xr loopctl 8
and
.Xr mount 8 .
.Pp
Supported devices include ATA and AHCI disks; USB keyboards, mice, and
flash drives through xHCI, on root ports or behind hubs; RTL8139,
e1000 (Intel 82540EM), and RTL8168 network cards; PS/2 keyboards and mice;
VGA text and mode 13h graphics; COM1 serial; Sound Blaster 16,
Intel HDA, and the PC speaker.
.Pp
Rach2 does not implement UEFI, Multiboot2, SMP, threads, swap,
dynamic linking, IPv6, or VESA graphics.
Every program is statically linked.
.Ss Images
.Bl -tag -width rach2-metal-disk
.It test
Guest probes.
.It os-simple
The project's init, login, su, passwd, and adduser programs.
.It os-real
BusyBox shell, login, and su, Dropbear, the compiler, and project sources.
.It rach2-metal-disk
os-real for an installed disk, with init-metal supervising Dropbear.
.It recovery
A RAM system with the installer and repair tools.
.El
.Ss The manual
The sections are:
.Bl -tag -width 2n -compact
.It 1
Programs.
.It 2
System calls.
.It 4
Devices.
.It 5
File formats.
.It 7
Overviews:
.Xr disk 7 ,
.Xr limits 7 ,
.Xr memory 7 ,
and
.Xr recovery 7 .
.It 8
Administration:
.Xr bootctl 8 ,
.Xr growroot 8 ,
.Xr loopctl 8 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr rach2-install 8 ,
.Xr rach2-recover 8 ,
and
.Xr reflash 8 .
.El
.Pp
Use
.Xr man 1
to read the manual.
Pages are plain text under
.Pa /usr/share/man/catN ,
where
.Ar N
is the section number.
See
.Xr proc 5
for the kernel's files under
.Pa /proc .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/log/services
.It Pa /usr/share/man
Manual pages.
.It Pa /src
Kernel, utility, and shell sources on images with a compiler.
.It Pa /proc
Kernel counters and tables.
.It Pa /dev
Device nodes.
.It Pa /etc/rach2
System configuration, including
.Pa limits
and
.Pa sshd.conf .
.It Pa /var/log/services
Output from init's services.
.It Pa /dev/bootlog
This boot's kernel log, readable by root.
.El
